  "review_findings": [
    "Both selected QAP-1 methods implement compiled robust tabu search with two nogil CPU workers. These are conventional algorithms; different budgets, seeds, tabu rules and perturbations prevent single-factor attribution.",
    "Candidate recomputes current/best objectives and rebuilds swap deltas after each 4000-iteration chunk, perturbing the incumbent on stagnation. Its 700-second nominal split budget gives 25 seconds per instance for development/confirmation and 21.875 seconds for the 64-instance audit, with an 820-second overall cap checked between chunks.",
    "Candidate train() probes development_features[0], not a training instance. Its objective sanity check uses feature-only optimization inputs and is not independent quality evidence; no learned state is fitted.",
    "Control rebuilds delta values at each phase start and exactly recomputes promising incumbent costs. It perturbs the best permutation, and uses full randomized restarts after repeated stagnation. Its per-instance allocation is 25 seconds for all three evaluated split sizes; time is checked between adaptive iteration chunks.",
    "Control train() checks four train instances for its solver but only two for an eight-restart scipy comparator. The two reported aggregate means use different sample counts and must not be directly compared; the reported 6.28 percent pairwise relative gain uses only the matched first two. The common frozen reference uses sixteen restarts.",
    "Content/index-derived random seeds do not make wall-time-budgeted searches bitwise deterministic. Claimed throughput or novelty in source docstrings is not treated as measured research ability.",
    "Optimization-family wall-time improvements are scoped to these two generated problem classes and two repetitions. They do not establish generic creativity or satisfy the unchanged whole-campaign/default gate."
  ],
